---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Pre"
  description="Terms of Service for Pre, the sport-specific prehab app."
>
  <main style="background-color: var(--color-bg); min-height: 100svh;">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm font-medium"
          style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);"
        >&larr; Back to Pre</a>
        <h1
          class="mb-4 font-sans text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl"
          style="color: var(--color-text);"
        >Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);">
          Effective date: May 21, 2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-prose" style="font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--color-text);">

        <p>
          These are the terms for using Pre, the sport-specific prehab app made by Borcsik Richárd
          e.v., a sole proprietor (egyéni vállalkozó) registered in Hungary, which we call "TrainStack"
          here ("we", "us"). Registered address: 1022 Budapest, Tapolcsányi utca 10, Hungary.
          Registration number: 60495392. Tax number: 91107673-1-41. EU VAT: HU91107673. They're the
          agreement between you and us. We've tried to keep them readable. By using Pre, you're
          agreeing to them — so if something here doesn't sit right with you, please don't use the app.
        </p>

        <h2>What Pre is</h2>
        <p>
          Pre uses AI to build personalized prehab, movement-preparation, and general fitness sessions
          from what you tell it: your sports, your body-region capacity ratings, your training context,
          and your session history. It's a fitness and educational tool, not a clinician.
        </p>

        <h2>Pre is not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Pre is not a medical device, and it does not give medical advice, diagnosis, or
          treatment.</strong> The sessions, exercises, and recommendations it generates are for general
          fitness and educational purposes only. They're no substitute for advice from a doctor,
          physical therapist, or other qualified professional.
        </p>
        <p>
          Talk to a healthcare professional before starting any exercise program, especially if you have
          an injury or a medical condition. If something hurts, stop and get it looked at. You follow
          Pre's guidance at your own risk. There's more detail in our
          <a href="/health-disclaimer" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Health Disclaimer</a>, and it's
          worth reading.
        </p>

        <h2>Who can use Pre</h2>
        <p>
          You need to be at least 18 to use Pre, and by using it you confirm that you are. Pre collects
          sensitive health and fitness information, so this matters. If we learn that an account belongs
          to someone under 18, we may suspend or close it and delete the associated data, except where
          the law requires us to keep something.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You're responsible for keeping your login details private and for what happens under your
          account. If you think someone else is using it, tell us right away.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data and content</h2>
        <p>
          The data you put into Pre — your capacity ratings, sport preferences, session feedback, and
          the rest — stays yours. By using the app, you give us a limited, non-exclusive license to
          host, process, reproduce, and use that information as needed to operate, secure, support,
          improve, and comply with the law in connection with Pre. Our
          <a href="/privacy" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Privacy Policy</a> spells out exactly how
          we handle it.
        </p>

        <h2>About the AI-generated content</h2>
        <p>
          Pre's sessions and recommendations are produced by an AI system from your inputs and general
          exercise-science principles. We can't guarantee that what it generates is accurate, complete,
          or right for your particular situation. Use your judgment, and lean on a professional when it
          matters.
        </p>

        <h2>Using Pre responsibly</h2>
        <p>A few things we need you not to do:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Pre for anything unlawful</li>
          <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or pull source code out of the app</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the infrastructure Pre runs on</li>
          <li>Share your account credentials with anyone else</li>
          <li>Pass off Pre's AI-generated content as professional medical advice</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Subscriptions and payments</h2>
        <p>
          Some of Pre's features require a paid subscription. Subscriptions are sold and billed through
          the Apple App Store and are subject to Apple's terms. You manage and cancel them from your App
          Store account. For the full picture on trials, renewals, cancellation, and refunds, see our
          <a href="/refunds" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Subscriptions, Billing &amp; Refunds</a>
          page.
        </p>

        <h2>Apple and the App Store</h2>
        <p>
          When you get Pre through the Apple App Store, these terms are between you and TrainStack —
          Apple isn't a party to them. The app itself is also covered by Apple's standard Licensed
          Application End User License Agreement. Apple has no obligation to support or maintain Pre, and
          TrainStack, not Apple, is responsible for the app and for handling any claims about it
          (including product liability, legal compliance, and intellectual property claims), to the
          extent the law allows. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these terms
          and may enforce them against you.
        </p>

        <h2>What belongs to us</h2>
        <p>
          Pre — its design, code, software, prompts, session-generation system, interfaces, and branding — belongs to TrainStack and is protected by
          intellectual property law. These terms don't hand you any rights to our trademarks, logos, or
          other brand features.
        </p>

        <h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent the law allows, TrainStack isn't liable for indirect, incidental,
          special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits or revenue, arising from your
          use of Pre. Our total liability for any claim under these terms won't exceed the amount you
          paid for Pre through the Apple App Store in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these
          terms excludes or limits any liability
          that can't be excluded or limited under applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranties</h2>
        <p>
          Pre is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, whether express or
          implied — including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
          and non-infringement.
        </p>

        <h2>Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to cover and hold harmless TrainStack and anyone who works with us
          from claims, damages, or expenses that come out of your use of Pre or your breach of these
          terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Ending things</h2>
        <p>
          We can suspend or close your access if you break these terms. You can stop using Pre any time
          you want. When access ends, your right to use the app ends with it — but the parts of these
          terms that should outlast the relationship (like the liability and indemnification sections)
          stay in force.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. If we change something material, we'll let you
          know in the app or by email. If you keep using Pre after a change takes effect, that counts as
          accepting the new terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          Pre is operated from Hungary, and these terms are governed by Hungarian law and the EU law
          that applies there. If you are a consumer, this doesn't take away the protection of the
          mandatory consumer-protection laws of the country where you live — nothing in these terms
          removes rights you can't waive under your local law, and where the law gives you the right to
          bring a claim in your local courts, you keep it.
        </p>

        <h2>The fine print</h2>
        <p>
          If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the rest stay in force. These terms —
          together with our <a href="/privacy" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Privacy Policy</a>,
          <a href="/health-disclaimer" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Health Disclaimer</a>, and
          <a href="/refunds" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Subscriptions, Billing &amp; Refunds</a>
          page — are the entire agreement between you and us about Pre. If we don't enforce a part of
          these terms right away, that's not a waiver. We may transfer these terms to another company
          (for example, in a sale of the business); you can't transfer your rights under them without
          our consent.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          If anything here needs explaining, write to us at
          <a href="mailto:legal@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">legal@trypre.app</a>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-prose a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
